{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"109104","commit":"9f79d4399c6ae09e52a5c276150a935f7bf8a5ad","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The introduction of `TextStructExecutor` and its usage in various classes diverges from the intended design. Specifically:\n- The `handledTransportActionExecutorService` method returns `DIRECT_EXECUTOR_SERVICE`, bypassing the thread pool\u0027s generic executor. This contradicts the mapping\u0027s intent to use `threadPool.generic()`. This change can lead to performance issues and potential deadlocks, as tasks are executed directly on the calling thread without proper management by the thread pool.\n- The `execute` method in `TextStructExecutor` uses `threadPool.generic().execute`, which also contradicts the mapping\u0027s intent. The mapping suggests that `executor.execute` should handle asynchronous execution consistently across different classes, but the implementation directly uses `threadPool.generic()`. This introduces redundancy and potential inconsistencies in how tasks are executed.\n- The assertion in `buildTextStructureResponse` is added to ensure it runs on the correct thread. While the mapping includes this assertion, its placement and necessity need verification. If not correctly placed or if there are other methods that should have similar assertions, this can lead to concurrency issues.\n- The `doExecute` method in `TransportFindFieldStructureAction` uses `threadPool.generic().execute` directly instead of using `executor.execute`. This introduces inconsistency and potential errors, as tasks are not managed through a single point of control.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/text-structure/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/textstructure/transport/TextStructExecutor.java-DST-ADDITION-761-1905-TypeDeclaration","path":"x-pack/plugin/text-structure/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/textstructure/transport/TextStructExecutor.java","srcDst":"DST","content":"/**\n * workaround for https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/97916\n * TODO delete this entire class when we can\n */\npublic class TextStructExecutor {\n    private final ThreadPool threadPool;\n\n    @Inject\n    public TextStructExecutor(ThreadPool threadPool) {\n        this.threadPool \u003d threadPool;\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * when the workaround is removed, change the value in each consuming class\u0027s constructor passes to the super constructor from\n     * DIRECT_EXECUTOR_SERVICE back to threadpool.generic() so that we continue to fork off of the transport thread.\n     */\n    ExecutorService handledTransportActionExecutorService() {\n        return DIRECT_EXECUTOR_SERVICE;\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * when the workaround is removed, change the callers of this function to\n     * {@link ActionListener#completeWith(ActionListener, CheckedSupplier)}.\n     */\n    \u003cT\u003e void execute(ActionListener\u003cT\u003e listener, CheckedSupplier\u003cT, Exception\u003e supplier) {\n        threadPool.generic().execute(ActionRunnable.supply(listener, () -\u003e {\n            assert ThreadPool.assertCurrentThreadPool(GENERIC);\n            return supplier.get();\n        }));\n    }\n}","nodeType":"ADDITION","treeType":"TypeDeclaration","descendantSimpleNames":["TextStructExecutor","ThreadPool","threadPool","Inject","TextStructExecutor","ThreadPool","threadPool","threadPool","threadPool","ExecutorService","handledTransportActionExecutorService","DIRECT_EXECUTOR_SERVICE","ActionListener","completeWith","ActionListener","CheckedSupplier","T","execute","ActionListener","T","listener","CheckedSupplier","T","Exception","supplier","threadPool","generic","execute","ActionRunnable","supply","listener","ThreadPool","assertCurrentThreadPool","GENERIC","supplier","get"],"identifiers":["handledTransportActionExecutorService","TextStructExecutor","supplier","listener","threadPool","execute"],"startLine":21,"startLineOffset":0,"endLine":51,"endLineOffset":1,"length":1145,"subs":[]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/text-stru